{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בן הוא ל' בינה", :translit "ben hu lashon binah", :gloss "ben is an expression of understanding"} {:he "השתלש", :translit "hishtalesh", :gloss "be tripled"} {:he "אגר", :translit "agar", :gloss "gathered"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: בן read as לשון בינה (understanding)"}], :frame {:text "The court must assess the offender before lashes: they estimate how many lashes he can physically endure, then administer a number divisible so that the total (after adjustment) can be completed as prescribed (Makkot 22b). The assessment procedure is detailed in tractate Makkot. Deuteronomy 1:38 describes Joshua as filled with the spirit of wisdom, which the midrash expands to include binah (Sotah 14a, Devarim Rabbah 2:6). Agur son of Jakeh in Proverbs 30:1 is read midrashically: 'Agur' means he gathered, and 'Jakeh' relates to understanding, that he gathered understanding and brought it forth (Leviticus Rabbah 1:15).", :sources ["Makkot 22b" "Deuteronomy 1:38" "Sotah 14a" "Devarim Rabbah 2:6" "Proverbs 30:1" "Leviticus Rabbah 1:15"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והפילו בגימ' כפול", :translit "vehifilo be-gimatriya keful", :gloss "vehifilo in gematria is doubled"} {:he "כפולה", :translit "kefulah", :gloss "doubled"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "והפילו", :b "כפול"}], :frame {:text "The strap used for lashes must be made of calf-hide and donkey-hide and must be doubled over so that two straps strike at once (Makkot 22b). The Ba'al HaTurim derives this doubling from the gematria of והפילו.", :sources ["Makkot 22b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כדי", :translit "k'dei", :gloss "according to"} {:he "ב' במס' הכא", :translit "bet be-masorah kan", :gloss "two in the Masorah here"} {:he "והשיגה ידו ומצא כדי גאולתו", :translit "vehisigah yado umatza k'dei ge'ulato", :gloss "if his hand reaches and he finds enough for his redemption"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["כדי" "והשיגה ידו ומצא כדי גאולתו"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'and if his hand reaches and he finds enough for his redemption' (Leviticus 25:26) refers to the redemption of a Hebrew slave. The pairing of the two occurrences of כדי is read as teaching that the wicked one who receives lashes is redeemed and released from his punishment.", :sources ["Leviticus 25:26"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: בן read as לשון בינה (understanding)", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:a-value 137, :b-value 136, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "כפול", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "והפילו"} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["כדי" "והשיגה ידו ומצא כדי גאולתו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "כדי", :refs ["Leviticus 25:26" "Deuteronomy 25:2" "Judges 6:5" "Daniel 2:43" "Daniel 3:7" "Daniel 6:11" "Daniel 6:15" "Nehemiah 5:8"], :n 8, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והשיגה ידו ומצא כדי גאולתו", :refs ["Leviticus 25:26"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:11.322183063Z", :model "glm-5.2"}